    {
      "paperId": "/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-73539-5_21",
      "doi": "10.1007/978-3-030-73539-5_21",
      "title": "MBSE Adoption for Cabin Temperature Control System Design of Civil Aircraft",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Junjie Ye, Wei Guo, ... Liangyu Zhao"
        }
      ],
      "year": 2021,
      "abstract": "In recent years, Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE) is rising rapidly in Systems Engineering (SE) field. The process of MBSE adoption for cabin temperature control system design of Civil Aircraft is described. The temperature control system model consists of a discrete model and a continuum model, which are built respectively. And the discrete model is built by Systems Modeling Language (SysML), a graphical modeling language. A method for MBSE, MagicGrid, is employed during the establishment of the discrete model, which includes requirements analysis, function analysis, and system architecture analysis. The FMI-based co-simulation of discrete model and continuum model are carried out to integrate the two models to support model verification, validation and iteration.",
